<section style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);">
  <div style="max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto;padding:52px 32px;">
    <h2 class="hana-h3" style="margin-bottom:22px;">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;max-width:860px;">
      <details class="loc-faq" open>
        <summary>What does Hana's Ayutthaya plant manufacture?<span class="loc-faq-mk" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="loc-faq-a">Ayutthaya is Hana's main OSAT plant in Thailand. It packages and tests low to medium pin-count ICs in leaded, leadless and custom packages, assembles optical and MEMS sensors, and also runs SMT, chip on board and box build. Products include automotive sensor packages, optical and ambient-light sensors, RF and microwave packages and power packages.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="loc-faq">
        <summary>Which certifications does the Ayutthaya plant hold?<span class="loc-faq-mk" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="loc-faq-a">IATF 16949, ISO 9001, ISO 14001, ISO 45001, ANSI/ESD S20.20, ISO/IEC 27001 and ISO 13485. The plant is also a Sony Green Partner and is approved for ITAR products. Full certificates are available on request.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="loc-faq">
        <summary>Where is the Ayutthaya plant?<span class="loc-faq-mk" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="loc-faq-a">In the Hi-Tech Industrial Estate at Bang Pa-in, Ayutthaya Province, central Thailand. It is about 40 km from Don Mueang Airport, 60 km from Suvarnabhumi International Airport and 130 km from the deep-sea port at Laem Chabang.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

